From 2d64b99ba2b59faaeba08c6ce2c01534a67c5539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:10:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] Lab: XCL_VIEW_FULL_RANGE=1 loads view ranges to their
 real end, counted either way

view_mem loaded 1 MiB behind a root address (XCL_VIEW_ROOT_KB) and a V#'s
records x stride up to 16 MiB; past that a tile never mapped read 0 and one
mapped by another draw kept its last copy. The VIctory fork kelvaroq
(stellarr-studio/kelvaroq, GPL-3.0, on fxceless/victory-fork f85101b) found
the same 1 MiB root view bound behind its "exploded triangles" and lets the
view cover the rest of the buffer; the idea is taken from there, the code is
XCL's own.

Behind a lab switch, OFF by default (FULL_RANGE_BY_DEFAULT: one line to turn
it on); without it the tiles looked at and copied are the same as before.
With it the size of a range comes from, in this order:
- the title's allocation that holds it, when XCL knows one
  (real::outside_buffer_left: buffers placed by CreatePlacedResourceX
  outside the windows);
- a V#'s own records x stride, without the 16 MiB bound;
- else (a root, a V# over 16 MiB) the end of the run of tiles from the
  first one that have a source, never short of the old bounds;
- at most XCL_VIEW_FULL_MB (256; 0: no cap) for the 1 GB pool's sake.
A tile without a source past the old bound ends the range and is not
counted as "without a source".

XCL_VIEW_FRESH_MS (1000, as before) sets how long a range or a tile is not
looked at again. The stats line keeps its text and adds, atomics only: roots
named / looked at / with a sourced tile right past XCL_VIEW_ROOT_KB (cut short
without the switch), V#s over 16 MiB, MB past the old bounds and what gave
each size (allocation, V#, sourced tiles, cap), ranges and tiles skipped as
fresh, pool-full rounds and tiles refused.

No draw-level size (vertex count, max index) reaches ensure_for_draw: mesh
draws carry none, so that source is not used.

view_mem.rs and real.rs are not in build.rs TRANSLATOR_SOURCES: the
translated identity stays 793bcfdace7b0c74.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
